oes when she leaves from there and the  TV show they kind of use Tyrion as a  buffer where he's better at politics so  you know he was able to at least work  together with her and there's a lot of  people who dislike her just because she  has dragons and it's kind of this  irrational thing of like oh well none of  the other characters have dragons so we  like them better or something silly like  that but there still is an underlying  problem with that apartment it's a  problem of magic in general which I'll  get into in a video later on in this  series but regardless of which side of  whether you're a Daenerys fan or your  Daenerys hater  she isn't necessarily the right fit  based on that thing that she had nothing  to do with and that was that she was  born into that family Daario says to her  you know you're not a ruler you're a  conqueror and that's not necessarily her  fault but it still is important in her  story where she's most effective is when  she uses that power and that's always in  the background of what she wants to do  for it it's worth I think that she has  the right kind of ideas the kind of  ideas that are inspiring you know  stopping slavery and making the world  better in that way but having the  ability to really bring those things to  task it causes a lot of backlash and  we've seen that whether it's in the  books or on the show you know people  aren't going to just go along because  they respect her power they're going to  fight back people are going to die and  if we look at what happened with her in  the east and we apply that to Westeros  is it really gonna be all that much  different there's a couple other  problems that come up when we think  about her in the endgame and those are  practical problems the first is related  to what we've just been talking about  but she isn't actually the heir to the  throne after all and she is gonna find  that out because she happens to be in a  relationship with the rightful heir of  course he is actuall